@startuml
title F02 - Resident consent and privacy controls
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam ArrowColor #2877B5
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #17324D
skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor #F4F7FA
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFF1BF
skinparam NoteBorderColor #9C6500
autonumber
actor "Resident" as Resident
control "H06\nHub resident interface" as H06
control "H07\nHub lifecycle/config" as H07
control "B02\nHome/consent" as B02
control "B08\nOperations/data" as B08
boundary "A01\nApp onboarding" as A01
Resident -> H06: Move the physical privacy control
H06 -> H07: Create explicit PRIVACY mode command
H07 -> H07: Atomically apply local mode/version
H07 -> B02: Synchronize privacy state when connectivity is available
B02 -> B08: Audit source, actor, version and effective time
B02 -> A01: Return consent/privacy state for caregiver view
A01 -> B02: Optional resident-consent withdrawal command
B02 -> H07: Publish privacy configuration; never silently resume
note over Resident,A01: Privacy suppresses missing-activity alerts; the UI must not present false reassurance.
note over Resident,A01: Outcome - Physical and remote consent changes converge on an auditable privacy state without pretending monitoring is active.
@enduml
